# market data — never committed. The manifest and the report are.
data/**/*.parquet
data/**/*.csv
data/fetch_log.jsonl
!data/manifest.json
!data/DATA-REPORT.md

# secrets. The real defence is that nothing secret is written inside the repo at
# all (DECISIONS.md D-015, D-017) and that tools/check_no_secrets.py scans content.
# This list is the second lock, and it is deliberately narrow.
#
# It used to contain `**/*secret*` and `**/*credential*`. Those matched on FILENAME,
# which buys nothing — a key pasted into notes.md is not called "secret" — and they
# silently ignored `tools/check_no_secrets.py`, so the scanner would never have been
# committed and nobody would have noticed. Content scanning is the real check.
.env
.env.*
*.env
!.env.example
**/kite_token.json
access_token*

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# session state and generated reports
state/
reports/
